            <ArticleTitle>Extraction atherectomy during myocardial infarction in a patient with prior coronary artery bypass surgery.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>117-21</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In this case report of a patient presenting with an acute inferior wall myocardial infarction, the infarct conduit was a saphenous vein graft. Extraction atherectomy using the TEC successfully reestablished patency and reversed the patient's clinical symptoms. Extraction atherectomy is a feasible procedure during acute coronary events and deserves further investigation.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
